# This repository is written on Windows and runs on Linux. `core.autocrlf=true` checks text files
# out with CRLF, which is harmless for most of them and fatal for a few: a shell script whose
# shebang ends `#!/bin/sh\r` makes the kernel look for an interpreter named `/bin/sh\r`, and the
# error it reports is "no such file or directory" — naming the script, not the interpreter, which
# sends you hunting for a missing file that is right there. That cost this project one failed
# publish on the first real deployment, 2026-09-19.
#
# Everything that is read by Linux — directly, or through a Docker image — is pinned to LF here.

*.sh            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
.env.prod.example text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to translate line endings inside them.
*.ttf           binary
*.png           binary
*.ico           binary
*.zip           binary
*.7z            binary
*.gz            binary
*.dump          binary
